| The same rule for a handler, which is where it used to leak: a handler
| defined in a linked file used to be handed the *program's* top level rather
| than its own file's, so it could read a name out here while being blind to
| the one written directly above it. Both halves of that are fixed; this
| holds the half that must stay refused.
let secret = 5

link "modules/handler_peeks_upward.code"

emit Peek {} to this get r
